ave been using property attribute for some metadata using non-BCL class and I got Serialization exception per documentation of PropertyAttribute constructor:\n\n> Constructor for use by derived classes that use the name of the type as the property name. Derived classes must ensure that the Type of the property value is a standard type supported by the BCL. Any custom types will cause a serialization Exception when in the client.\n\nWe have been using ReSharper to run our unit tests and the tests worked there so it took a while to track it down (we have tried NUnit GUI runner and Visual Studio Adapter). More helpful error message or perhaps even exception thrown from the constructor would be nice.\n\n```\n    [AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Method, AllowMultiple = true)]\n    public class LoginAsAttribute : PropertyAttribute\n    {\n        public LoginAsAttribute(Role role) : base(role)\n        {\n        }\n    }\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"rprouse","id":493828,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MzgyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/493828?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse","html_url":"https://github.com/rprouse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rprouse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nunit/nunit/issues/360/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":